---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ProductWindow from "../components/ProductWindow.astro";
import FeatureArt from "../components/FeatureArt.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Bitlab — A simple, fast AI workspace powered by Pi" description="Bitlab is a simple, fast, local-first AI workspace powered by the Pi agent runtime for Desktop and WebUI.">
  <section class="shell hero">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Powered by Pi agent</div>
        <h1>Simple. Fast. Ready to work.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Bitlab pairs the lightweight Pi agent runtime with a local-first workspace that feels quick, clear, and easy to use — sessions, files, and credentials stay on your machine.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/limboinf/bitlab-agent/releases/latest">Download Bitlab</a>
          <a class="button button-quiet" href="https://github.com/limboinf/bitlab-agent">View source ↗</a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-note">Desktop · WebUI &nbsp; / &nbsp; Open source under Apache-2.0</p>
      </div>
      <ProductWindow lang="en" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell section product-showcase" id="product">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>The real workspace.<br />Ready for real work.</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Move from conversation to finished artifacts, connect the tools you already use, and keep reusable workflows close at hand — all inside Bitlab.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="screenshot-grid">
      <article class="screenshot-card screenshot-card-primary">
        <div class="screenshot-frame">
          <img src="/assets/screenshots/agent-artifact-preview.webp" alt="Bitlab generating and previewing an interactive release artifact inside an agent session" width="3152" height="2152" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <h3>From a prompt to a working artifact</h3>
        <p>Follow the agent’s progress, inspect its file operations, and preview the finished result without leaving the session.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="screenshot-card">
        <div class="screenshot-frame">
          <img src="/assets/screenshots/mcp-connectors.webp" alt="Bitlab MCP connector manager showing installed external tool servers" width="3152" height="2152" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <h3>Connect external tools</h3>
        <p>Manage MCP servers, tool availability, and connection status from one clear workspace.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="screenshot-card">
        <div class="screenshot-frame">
          <img src="/assets/screenshots/skills-library.webp" alt="Bitlab Skills library showing reusable agent capabilities" width="3152" height="2152" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <h3>Reuse the way you work</h3>
        <p>Browse, import, and enable Skills that package trusted instructions, scripts, and references.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell section" id="features">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>Less ceremony.<br />More useful work.</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Pi handles the agent loop. Bitlab gives it a calm home: local-first workspaces, explicit permissions, model connections, MCP servers, Skills, plus a browser and office tools built in.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-list">
      <article class="feature"><FeatureArt pos="tr" /><span class="feature-index">01</span><h3>Connect models your way</h3><p>Sign in with ChatGPT Plus, use API keys for providers such as OpenAI or Anthropic (Claude), connect OpenAI- or Anthropic-compatible endpoints, or run local Ollama models. One picker sets the connection, model, and thinking level — and remembers your choice.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><FeatureArt pos="bl" /><span class="feature-index">02</span><h3>MCP connectors</h3><p>Add Model Context Protocol servers per workspace over stdio, SSE, or streamable HTTP. Remote servers authorize over OAuth and refresh their own tokens; tools from an untrusted server ask before they run.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><FeatureArt pos="tr" /><span class="feature-index">03</span><h3>Skills for repeated work</h3><p>Package instructions, scripts, and references as Skills in the open Agent Skills format — the same Skill also loads in Codex and Claude Code. Pick one from the chat, or let the model find it when the task fits.</p></article>
      <article class="feature"><FeatureArt pos="bl" /><span class="feature-index">04</span><h3>Browser and office tools built in</h3><p>The agent researches, fills forms, and extracts data in a browser pane beside the chat, with web search ready out of the box. Document tools handle PDF, Word, Excel, and slides, so everyday office work gets done without switching apps.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell section" id="principles">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="manifesto"><p>Good agent software should get out of the way quickly — then remember where you left off.</p></div>
      <div class="principles">
        <div class="principle"><b>01</b><span>Pi keeps the agent loop small and adaptable.</span></div>
        <div class="principle"><b>02</b><span>Explore, Ask, Execute — permission modes stay explicit, and credentials live in your OS keychain.</span></div>
        <div class="principle"><b>03</b><span>Local-first data means less setup, every time.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="download">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="eyebrow">Ready when you are</div>
      <h2>Start with a faster path to useful work.</h2>
      <p>Download the latest release, or explore the source behind Bitlab and its Pi-powered runtime.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/limboinf/bitlab-agent/releases/latest">Get the latest release</a>
        <a class="button button-quiet" href="https://github.com/limboinf/bitlab-agent/blob/main/docs/README.md">Read the docs ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
